IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rbw-retrenchment-workfare`

-- Retrenchment benefit (Tripartite Advisory, as MOM publishes it) and the Workfare Income Supplement (as the CPF Board
-- publishes it) -- worked cases. AS PUBLISHED, NOT LAW. Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING of the pages read on
-- 12 October 2026, not about the law.

§ `Fixtures`

-- A citizen employee with an ordinary household: home annual value $15,000, one property, not married.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, worked IS A BOOLEAN, income IS A NUMBER, average IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Worker
`an employee` age worked income average MEANS
    Worker WITH
        `Singapore Citizen` IS TRUE
        `age at 31 December of the work year` IS age
        `person with disabilities` IS FALSE
        `ComCare Short-to-Medium-Term Assistance recipient or qualifying caregiver` IS FALSE
        `worked as an employee in the month` IS worked
        `gross income for the month` IS income
        `average gross monthly income over the past 12 months` IS average
        `annual value of home at 31 December of the preceding year` IS 15000
        `properties owned, with spouse if married` IS 1
        married IS FALSE
        `spouse's assessable income for the preceding Year of Assessment` IS 0

-- An employee aged 25 or 40 earning $400 a month, with or without a concessionary status.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, disabled IS A BOOLEAN, concession IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Worker
`a low earner` age disabled concession MEANS
    Worker WITH
        `Singapore Citizen` IS TRUE
        `age at 31 December of the work year` IS age
        `person with disabilities` IS disabled
        `ComCare Short-to-Medium-Term Assistance recipient or qualifying caregiver` IS concession
        `worked as an employee in the month` IS TRUE
        `gross income for the month` IS 400
        `average gross monthly income over the past 12 months` IS 400
        `annual value of home at 31 December of the preceding year` IS 15000
        `properties owned, with spouse if married` IS 1
        married IS FALSE
        `spouse's assessable income for the preceding Year of Assessment` IS 0

-- A 49-year-old earning $2,500 (average $2,500), with the household facts varied.
GIVEN `annual value` IS A NUMBER, properties IS A NUMBER, `is married` IS A BOOLEAN, `spouse income` IS A NUMBER, citizen IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Worker
`a household` `annual value` properties `is married` `spouse income` citizen MEANS
    Worker WITH
        `Singapore Citizen` IS citizen
        `age at 31 December of the work year` IS 49
        `person with disabilities` IS FALSE
        `ComCare Short-to-Medium-Term Assistance recipient or qualifying caregiver` IS FALSE
        `worked as an employee in the month` IS TRUE
        `gross income for the month` IS 2500
        `average gross monthly income over the past 12 months` IS 2500
        `annual value of home at 31 December of the preceding year` IS `annual value`
        `properties owned, with spouse if married` IS properties
        married IS `is married`
        `spouse's assessable income for the preceding Year of Assessment` IS `spouse income`

§ `REQ-0276 (cradle-to-grave-jun-hao j087, 30 November 2055)`

-- The scenario is in 2055; these answers are on the policy AS PUBLISHED IN OCTOBER 2026 (Advisory updated 20 January 2023;
-- WIS tables for Work Year 2025, cap repeated for 2026), on the assumption that nothing changes.

-- 21 years' service: eligible under the Advisory (2 years or more).
#ASSERT `eligible for retrenchment benefit under the Advisory` 21

-- The norm: two weeks to one month's salary per year of service. Bottom (two weeks read as half a month): 21 x $1,550 =
-- $32,550. Top: 21 x $3,100 = $65,100.
#ASSERT `the bottom of the Advisory's norm` 3100 21 EQUALS 32550
#ASSERT `the top of the Advisory's norm` 3100 21 EQUALS 65100

-- If his union's collective agreement stipulates the quantum: one month per year, $65,100.
#ASSERT `the Advisory's norm where a collective agreement stipulates the quantum` 3100 21 TRUE EQUALS 65100

-- MOM: "not mandated by law" -- the ledger's premise that the Act entitles him is not what the publisher says.
#ASSERT NOT `retrenchment benefit is mandated by law, as MOM publishes it`

-- Workfare for November 2055, his last month of work at $3,100: nothing; $3,100 is above the $3,000 cap.
#ASSERT NOT `qualifies for employee WIS for the month` (`an employee` 49 TRUE 3100 3100) 2055

-- December 2055, unemployed after retrenchment: nothing; WIS is paid only for months worked.
#ASSERT NOT `qualifies for employee WIS for the month` (`an employee` 49 FALSE 0 3100) 2055

-- Had he qualified, his age band (45 to 59) caps WIS at $4,200 a year: $1,680 cash and $2,520 to CPF.
#ASSERT `the maximum yearly employee WIS` (`an employee` 49 TRUE 3100 3100) 2055 EQUALS 4200
#ASSERT `the cash part of employee WIS` 4200 EQUALS 1680
#ASSERT `the CPF part of employee WIS` 4200 EQUALS 2520

-- If he is re-employed in 2056 at $2,800 and his 12-month average is $2,900, he qualifies again; if the average is still
-- $3,050, he does not.
#ASSERT `qualifies for employee WIS for the month` (`an employee` 50 TRUE 2800 2900) 2056
#ASSERT NOT `qualifies for employee WIS for the month` (`an employee` 50 TRUE 2800 3050) 2056

§ `Retrenchment benefit -- eligibility and norm`

#ASSERT NOT `eligible for retrenchment benefit under the Advisory` 1.5
#ASSERT `eligible for retrenchment benefit under the Advisory` 2
#ASSERT `the bottom of the Advisory's norm` 3100 2 EQUALS 3100
#ASSERT `the top of the Advisory's norm` 3100 2 EQUALS 6200

-- Two weeks' salary on the two readings: $3,100 / 2 = $1,550; $2,600 x 12 / 26 = $1,200.
#ASSERT `two weeks' salary, read as half a month` 3100 EQUALS 1550
#ASSERT `two weeks' salary, reckoned as a twenty-sixth of a year's pay` 2600 EQUALS 1200

-- Within the norm for 21 years at $3,100 ($32,550 to $65,100)?
#ASSERT `the sum is within the Advisory's norm` 40000 3100 21
#ASSERT NOT `the sum is within the Advisory's norm` 30000 3100 21

-- A salary cut shortly before: computed on the pre-cut $3,100, not $2,800.
#ASSERT `the salary to compute retrenchment benefit on` 2800 3100 TRUE EQUALS 3100

-- 63 and over: the Employee Assistance Payment may be used, unless the contract provides retrenchment benefit.
#ASSERT `the employer may use the Employee Assistance Payment instead` 63 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the employer may use the Employee Assistance Payment instead` 63 TRUE

#ASSERT NOT `CPF contributions are payable on retrenchment benefit`
#ASSERT `a TADM claim is in time` 6

§ `Workfare -- income cap, floor and age`

#ASSERT `the WIS income cap` 2026 EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `qualifies for employee WIS for the month` (`an employee` 40 TRUE 3000 3000) 2025
#ASSERT NOT `qualifies for employee WIS for the month` (`an employee` 40 TRUE 2600 2600) 2024
#ASSERT NOT `qualifies for employee WIS for the month` (`an employee` 29 TRUE 2000 2000) 2025
#ASSERT NOT `qualifies for employee WIS for the month` (`a low earner` 40 FALSE FALSE) 2025
#ASSERT `qualifies for employee WIS for the month` (`a low earner` 25 TRUE FALSE) 2025
#ASSERT `qualifies for employee WIS for the month` (`a low earner` 40 FALSE TRUE) 2025
-- Work Year 2023: no figures on the pages read.
#ASSERT NOT `qualifies for employee WIS for the month` (`an employee` 40 TRUE 2000 2000) 2023

§ `Workfare -- household conditions`

#ASSERT `qualifies for employee WIS for the month` (`a household` 21000 1 FALSE 0 TRUE) 2025
#ASSERT NOT `qualifies for employee WIS for the month` (`a household` 21001 1 FALSE 0 TRUE) 2025
#ASSERT NOT `qualifies for employee WIS for the month` (`a household` 15000 1 TRUE 70001 TRUE) 2025
#ASSERT NOT `qualifies for employee WIS for the month` (`a household` 15000 1 FALSE 0 FALSE) 2025

§ `Workfare -- maximum payouts, split and timing`

#ASSERT `the maximum yearly employee WIS for the age` 30 2025 EQUALS 2450
#ASSERT `the maximum yearly employee WIS for the age` 44 2025 EQUALS 3500
#ASSERT `the maximum yearly employee WIS for the age` 60 2025 EQUALS 4900
-- A person with disabilities aged 25 gets the 60-and-above amount.
#ASSERT `the maximum yearly employee WIS` (`a low earner` 25 TRUE FALSE) 2025 EQUALS 4900
#ASSERT `the maximum yearly self-employed WIS for the age` 49 2025 EQUALS 2800
#ASSERT `the cash part of self-employed WIS` 2800 EQUALS 280
-- January work is paid by end March; December 2055 work would be paid by end February 2056.
#ASSERT `the month WIS for the work month is paid by` 1 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the month WIS for the work month is paid by` 12 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the year WIS for the work month is paid by` 12 2055 EQUALS 2056
